SASMs is currently known or conjectured.\n\n26 ILSE FISCHER AND MANJIL P. SAIKIA\n\nx 1¯x 1 x 2¯x 2\n\nqx 1\n\nqx 2\n\nFigure 10. The grid corresponding to VOSASMs.\n\nTheorem 7.1.\n\nZ UO(n;x 1, x 2, . . . , x 2 n) =\n\nσ(q 2)3 n−8 n 2 σ(q)2 n Q i≤2 n σ(q 2 x 2\n\ni)\n\nQ i<j≤2 n σ(¯x i x j)2 Q i≤j≤2 n σ(x i x j)2 Y\n\ni<j≤2 n\n\nσ(q¯x i x j)2 σ(qx i¯x j)2 σ(qx i x j)2 σ(q¯x i¯x j)2\n\n×Pf 1≤i<j≤2 nσ(¯x i x j)σ(x i x j)1\n\nspectral parameters ~x, which was found by Aval and Duchon [AD10] (up to some normalization\n\nfactor).\n\nWe now use the following result of Aval and Duchon [AD10, Theorem 6], if q+ ¯q= 1 then\n\nwe have\n\nZ qQ(4 n+ 2; x, 1,...,1) = Z(n;x, 1,...,1)Z(n+ 1; x, 1,...,1)Z H(2 n+ 1; x, 1,...,1).(9.2)\n\nCombining equations (9.1),(8.2),(8.3) and (9.2) we obtain the result. \n\n10. Concluding Remarks\n\nIn this paper, we have proved several results for reﬁned enumeration of symmetry classes\n\nof ASMs. We summarize the results so far in the literature for singly reﬁned enumeration of\n\nsymmetry classes of ASMs below.\n\n•Unrestricted ASMs. First enumerated by Zeilberger [Zei96a]. The reﬁned enumeration\n\nwith respect to ﬁrst row is also due to Zeilberger [Zei96b].\n\n•VSASMs. Enumerated by Kuperberg [Kup02], singly reﬁned enumeration with respect\n\nto the ﬁrst column was accomplished by Razumov and Stroganov [RS06a], while the\n\nsingly reﬁned enumeration with respect to the second row is obtained in this paper.\n\n•VHSASMs. Enumerated by Okada [Oka06]. Generating function for singly reﬁned\n\nenumeration with respect to the second row provided in this paper.\n\n•HTSASMs. For even order enumerated by Kuperberg [Kup02] and for odd order by\n\nRazumov and Stroganov [RS06b]. Singly reﬁned enumeration done by Stroganov [Str06].\n\n•QTSASMs. Enumerated by Kuperberg [Kup02] for order n≡0 (mod 4) and by Razu-\n\nmov and Stroganov [RS06b] for order n≡1 (mod 2). Reﬁned enumeration results\n\nproved in this paper.\n\n•Diagonally Symmetric ASMs. No formula known or conjectured.\n\n•DADSASMs. For odd order enumerated by Behrend, Fischer and Konvalinka [BFK17].\n\n•TSASMs. No formula known or conjectured.\n\nAs can be seen from the list, our results almost exhaust the singly reﬁned enumeration possi-\n\nbilities for the symmetry classes of ASMs. Double reﬁnement by ﬁxing the positions of the 1s\n\nin two rows or columns have been studied only for the case of unrestricted ASMs. Some other\n\ndoubly reﬁned enumeration possibilities still remain, for instance doubly reﬁned enumeration\n\nof VSASMs with the positions of the ﬁrst 1 in the second row and the unique 1 in the ﬁrst\n\ncolumn ﬁxed. However, no conjectures for such cases are known at the moment. We refer the\n\n36 ILSE FISCHER AND MANJIL P. SAIKIA\n\nreader to Behrend, Fischer and Konvalinka’s paper [BFK17, Section 1.2] for a survey of all such\n\nknown or conjectured results.\n\nIn addition to the symmetry classes, the following closely related classes have been studied\n\nin the literature (as well as this paper).\n\n•qQTSASMs. Enumerated by Aval and Duchon [AD10]. Reﬁned enumeration results\n\nproved in this paper.\n\n•OSASMs. For even order enumerated by Kuperberg [Kup02] and reﬁned enumeration\n\nby Razumov and Stroganov [RS06a].\n\n•OOSASMs. For even order no formula is known or conjectured. For odd order enumer-\n\nated by Ayyer, Behrend and Fischer [ABF20], reﬁned enumeration results in terms of\n\ngenerating function proved in this paper.\n\n•VOSASMs. Enumerated by Okada [Oka06] and reﬁned enumeration results in terms of\n\ngenerating function proved in this paper.\n\nWe would like to close the paper by posing the following problems.\n\n(1) Bijective proofs of equations (3.12), (5.11), (6.7) and (6.8) would be interesting.\n\n(2) The number A VC(2 n+ 1, i) of vertically symmetric ASMs with the unique 1 in the ﬁrst\n\ncolumn situated in the i-th row equals A O(2 n, i) (this follows from the work of Razumov\n\nand Stroganov [RS04]). This gives us\n\nA V(2 n+ 1, i) = A VC(2 n+ 1, i)+A VC(2 n+ 1, i + 1).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFactorization of rational six vertex model partition functions | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/385897594_Factorization_of_rational_six_vertex_model_partition_functions)\nciteturn3search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; In a previous article [math.CO/9712207], we derived the alternating-sign matrix (ASM) theorem from the Izergin-Korepin determinant for a partition function for square ice with domain wall boundary. Here we show that the same argument enumerates three other symmetry classes of alternating-sign matrices: VSASMs (vertically symmetric ASMs), even HTSASMs (half-turn-symmetric ASMs), and even QTSASMs (quarter-turn-symmetric ASMs). The VSASM enumeration was conjectured by Mills; the others by Robbins [math.CO/0008045].\nSymmetry Classes of Alternating-Sign Matrices under One Roof\n\nArticle\n\n  * Sep 2000\n  * ANN MATH\n\n  * Greg Kuperberg\n\nIn a previous article [math.CO/9712207], we derived the alternating-sign matrix (ASM) theorem from the Izergin-Korepin determinant for a partition function for square ice with domain wall boundary. Here we show that the same argument enumerates three other symmetry classes of alternating-sign matrices: VSASMs (vertically symmetric ASMs), even HTSASMs (half-turn-symmetric ASMs), and even QTSASMs (quarter-turn-symmetric ASMs). The VSASM enumeration was conjectured by Mills; the others by Robbins [math.CO/0008045]. We introduce several new types of ASMs: UASMs (ASMs with a U-turn side), UUASMs (two U-turn sides), OSASMs (off-diagonally symmetric ASMs), OOSASMs (off-diagonally, off-antidiagonally symmetric), and UOSASMs (off-diagonally symmetric with U-turn sides). UASMs generalize VSASMs, while UUASMs generalize VHSASMs (vertically and horizontally symmetric ASMs) and another new class, VHPASMs (vertically and horizontally perverse). OSASMs, OOSASMs, and UOSASMs are related to the remaining symmetry classes of ASMs, namely DSASMs (diagonally symmetric), DASASMs (diagonally, anti-diagonally symmetric), and TSASMs (totally symmetric ASMs). We enumerate several of these new classes, and we provide several 2-enumerations and 3-enumerations. Our main technical tool is a set of multi-parameter determinant and Pfaffian formulas generalizing the Izergin-Korepin determinant for ASMs and the Tsuchiya determinant for UASMs [solv-int/9804010]. We evaluate specializations of the determinants and Pfaffians using the factor exhaustion method.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQuestions — MathDB (https://mathdb.com/questions?tag=dyck-paths)\nciteturn3search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; open Open about 1 year · documented by 2025 dyck-paths hypergraph-decompositions symmetry ...   * ## Dyck-path strengthening of the wreath conjecture\nopenOpen about 1 year · documented by 2025dyck-pathshypergraph-decompositionssymmetry\n\n0 0 5\n\n  * ## Dyck-path strengthening of the wreath conjecture\n\nDyck-path strengthening. There exists a set $\\Pi=\\{\\pi_1,\\pi_2,\\ldots,\\pi_{C_k}\\}$Π={π 1​,π 2​,…,π C k​​} of $C_k$C k​ permutations of $\\mathbb{Z}_{2k+1}$Z 2 k+1​, each fixing $0$0, and a bijection…\n\nopenOpen about 1 year · documented by 2025catalan-numbersdyck-pathshypergraph-decompositions\n\n0 0 4\n\n  * ## Bóna–Dimitrov's Sturm-unimodality conjecture for Dyck-path polynomials\n\nLet $W_{n,k}(x)=\\sum_{m=0}^{k}w_{n,k,m}x^m$W n,k​(x)=∑m=0 k​w n,k,m​x m, where $w_{n,k,m}$w n,k,m​ counts Dyck paths of semilength $n$n with $k$k occurrences of $UD$U D and $m$m occurrences of $UUD$U U D. For real-rooted polyno…\n\nopenOpen about 3 years · documented by 2023combinatoricsdyck-pathsreal-rooted-polynomials\n\n0 0 3\n\n  * ## Bóna–Dimitrov's generalized Sturm sequence conjecture for Dyck-path polynomials\n\nLet $W_{n,k}(x)=\\sum_{m=0}^{k}w_{n,k,m}x^m$W n,k​(x)=∑m